# Drill into skipped jobs by reason
Workstream-ID: lea-28
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/28
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed bounded skip-history inspection improvement
Status: DONE
Milestone: Inspect every job counted by a skip-reason bar
Dependencies: lea-09

## Purpose
Make skip-reason bars open their complete matching event list in both dashboard
entry points. Show useful job identity and recorded decision context without
requiring an application record or revisiting LinkedIn.

## Tasks
- [x] Trace chart rendering, skip persistence, scoring and existing metadata.
- [x] Preserve preceding local work, tracking records and private runtime boundaries.
- [x] Add scoped bar selection, an accessible reason filter and complete matching lists.
- [x] Capture immutable job metadata, available decision-time scores and skip explanations.
- [x] Qualify migration, legacy/missing data, repeated events and real browser interaction.
- [x] Update affected guides and prepare only this workstream's completion projection.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Clicking a reason lists every corresponding recorded skip, newest first.
- [x] Bar counts and list membership agree beyond the former 5,000-event cutoff.
- [x] Repeated job skips remain distinct events, with timestamps and run identity.
- [x] Basic job information, links and available saved descriptions are inspectable.
- [x] Future decisions retain captured metadata and available scores/explanations.
- [x] Existing databases migrate additively; legacy or unavailable details are identified honestly.
- [x] Both skip-chart entry points work without stale selections or fixed column widths.
- [x] Dashboard inspection is read-only and does not create applications or browse LinkedIn.
- [x] Fictional fixtures preserve prior work, private inputs and independent applications.
- [x] One repository issue, one issue-backed Project item and a durable backlink represent the workstream.

## Completion evidence
Both dashboard entry points expose complete newest-first event lists through
selectable bars, a reason picker and Show all. Row checkboxes reveal recorded
posting details, decision explanations, available original scores and literal
descriptions; CSV downloads follow the selected reason. Counts retain repeated
events rather than silently deduplicating jobs.

An additive nullable context column preserves future observed posting metadata
and available decision-time evidence without requiring an application record.
Failed targets retain their available URL/title and form skips retain the
actual result reason. Legacy joins are labeled as current metadata; absent
historical fields stay unknown. Aggregate-only history cannot be reconstructed.

The initial focused batch passed 107 cases. After browser testing exposed
truthy missing-value inference, two failing-before-fix regressions were added
and all 22 dashboard cases passed with the object-dtype fix. Scoped Black,
Ruff and mypy passed. These are separate observed batches, not a claim that
109 combined cases were rerun after the final change.

Actual fictional browser qualification passed ten boundaries and 21 successful
backend completions across 5,006 events. A selected reason exported all 5,003
matching rows. Filtering, clearing, reselection, repeated captured decisions,
legacy/orphan/unknown records, both entry points and contained 430-pixel
scrolling were exercised. Selected/narrow captures were inspected. Fictional
database bytes stayed identical; no application, page error or external
request occurred.

Six affected guides are updated without expanding the short README. Bounded
source comparison preserves 114 original definitions outside the required
edits, ten unaffected prior public fingerprints, all 27 preceding workstream
sources/mappings, selected private metadata, unchanged HEAD and empty staging.
Both exact owned fixture processes are absent; only the inspected fictional
database and empty fixture directory were removed.

This is bounded local technical completion. Scoped tracking settlement is
recorded separately in the excluded index/ledger. Independent user applications
were not controlled. Live LinkedIn qualification, human acceptance and
source/release publication are not claimed or newly authorized.

